If the game tried to save, and went out of disk space, there's probably
no hope. However, try to rename the file to a .Z (or .gz) or whatever
extension you have on your compressed save files (I assume you didn't
undefine the compression part when you compiled it), since Nethack
looks for a compressed file. The .e file indicates that there were some
error when you tried to save, and since that file is 0 in length, the real
savefile (10me) probably hasn't got all data needed in it, so don't be
too optimistic.

